// E0012: a `/*` block comment with no closing `*/` runs to end-of-file.
// Without a diagnostic, this would silently swallow the rest of the file
// (including `main`) while the compiler still reports "No errors found"
// (exit 0) - a valid-looking build of a file that never compiled. The lexer
// emits a diagnostic here, matching the unterminated-string /
// unterminated-char handling.
![config(testing)]
![config(negative, E0012)]
namespace CryoTests::Negative::UnterminatedBlockComment;

function main() -> int {
    return 0;
}

/* this block comment is intentionally never closed
